I just wrote up a wishing spoiler. It maybe useful for beginners who
want to
make most of a wish. It is not a normal wishing spoiler. I don't
generally recommend
what to wish for but try to give an idea as to why you would want to
wish something.

Hoping for a good response from seasoned players.

-anandsr

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The most important use of Wishes is to make your character survive
longer.
First we will cover important attributes required to survive longer.


Magic Resistance
----------------
MR is only required after you have reached mid-game. It can become
painful from
Dungeon level 7, when Polymorph traps  and Level Teleport Traps start
to occur.
But these traps are not instant kills although they could be very
dangerous for
your character.  The polymorph  trap can  destroy your armour  if it
makes you
something big or make you naked and  vulnerable if you turn out to be
something
small. Level Teleport can send you on a different level in the middle
of a host
of monsters without your pet. But still they are not instant kills. If
you are
very unlucky a monster maybe generated with a wand of death.

There is no sure way to find MR randomly in the dungeon, except Cloak
of MR and
Gray Dragon Scales or Scale Mail.

Wizards start of with Cloak of MR.

Ways to wish for MR.
a) blessed +3 Grey Dragon Scale Mail (unless you have magic
resistance).
b) blessed greased fireproof +3 cloak of magic resistance (if you are a
monk see above).
c) You could also wish for a MR giving quest artifact. But they all
blast so
you should have at least 40 hit points. The good thing about these
quest
artifacts is that they usually have extra benefits and these are safe
items, in
the end game. The Wizard and other Nasties don't try to steal them.
Your own
quest item is not safe. And you can use your armour or cloak slot for
other
things.

For neutrals (that want to use spells) The Eye of the Aethiopica is the
best
option, except for Wizards who will get it anyway.
Other good artifacts are
- neutral The Platinum Yendorian Express Card: gives MR, telepathy,
charging.
- neutral The Eyes of the Overworld: MR, Astral Vision, Enlightenment.
  It also protects against any light based attacks.
- lawful  The sceptre of might: MR + Conflict (very useful)
- lawful  The magic mirror of merlin: MR + Telepathy.
- unfortunately nothing for chaotics, they could use MagicBane though.
Some consider Enlightenment+Astral Vision to be greater than Telepathy.
Charging is really mostly useful only for Tourist.
Also some consider Conflict as more important than Telepathy.

d) You could also wish for MagicBane and (remember to) wield it. It may
blast
non-neutrals so have atleast 24 hit points.


Poison Resistance
-----------------
PR is required as soon as possible as spiked pits and dart/arrow traps
are
found very early. When large Orcs start to appear you better have PR
otherwise
it is difficult to survive.

PR can be easily obtained by eating PR granting corpses (consult
monster
manual). Before you obtain Unicorn Horn however it is only advisable to
eat the
non-poisoness PR granting corpses.

Orcs, healer, barbarians, and tourists also start with it and Monks get
it at
XL3.

Ways to wish for PR
a) blessed +3 Green Dragon Scale Mail.
b) blessed tin of green dragon meet.


Reflection
----------
In addition you must also have Reflection.  Reflection prevents ray
based
attacks, like Wand of Death/Lightning/Fire/Cold etc. These ray attacks
do a lot
of damage.  If you have low hitpoints it may as well be an instant
kill.  Also
the monster will fire as many times it can. So it is nearly a
instakill, if you
don't have MR.  It also destroys a lot of stuff. It is important to get
it as
soon as possible.

There is a 50% probability of finding Amulet of Reflection in Sokoban,
and
another 50% probability of finding the shield of reflection in the
statue of
Perseus in Medusa's Island.

Ways to wish for Reflection
a) blessed +3 Silver Dragon Scale Mail (unless you also have
reflection, you
may still want to get it because you may want to use the amulet slot,
or you
want to cast spells). But it is still better to do a reverse genocide
of Silver
Dragons, during the mid-level game.
b) blessed amulet of reflection (if monk see above).
c) Longbow of Diana - Only useful for non-ranger Chaotics. It must be
wielded
to get reflection and will blast at every wielding.


Due to the difficulty of finding MR it is considered the highest
priority wish.
PR is not considered very important by most people except the very
seasoned
players. If you do get a Wand of Wishing it is important enough to
spend a wish
on it. Because you cannot let the good fortune of finding the WoW go to
waste.
Reflection comes in between the two in priority, because it is very
important
in the early game, and you may not find it eventually.


Armour
------
Armour is of prime importance, that is why you go on checking every
armour you
find to use the best available. But wishing for the best armour (a
dragon scale
mail) is not incompatible with wishing for the three above attributes.
So first
wish should be spend on a DSM giving an appropriate necessary
attribute.
Once you have a DSM it is better to wish for a magic marker (if you
haven't
found it already) before going for different magic armour. The magic
marker
will allow you to enchant your existing armour to high levels.


Magic Marker
------------
This is the most wished for item in the game. It can increase the
effectiveness
of your armours and weapons both. It should have a higher priority than
a good
artifact weapon.


Weapon
------
A good weapon comes very low on wishing priorities as the best strategy
to play
nethack is to not fight monsters directly but attack them from far. So
it is
better to have a long range attack than a good melee weapon.

The best weapons for wishing are
1) Grayswandir: Great all around weapon for anybody who can reach basic
in
this weapon. Difficult to get it unrestricted by sacrificing as the
only other
saber is Werebane. It doesn't destroy anything which makes it very
good. It is
not so bad even if restricted. The +5 to hit helps counter the
restriction. And
later with high luck restriction is not a problem.
2) Frost brand: More effective in the hell, but destroys potions. Very
easy to
get unrestricted for lawfuls and neutrals as they get Excalibur or
Vorpal blade
on crowning. Not so easy for chaotics.
3) Fire brand: More effective in the planes, but destroyes potions,
scrolls,
spellbooks. Very easy to get unrestricted for neutrals and lawfuls.
4) Mjollnir: More effective in the hell, but destroys rings and wands.
Easy to
get for Valkyries by sacrificing. It is also a good long range weapon
for
Valkyrie if you have Gauntlets of Power, but beware it is a trap, as 1
times in
hundred it will hit you, and when that happens you may loose your wands
and
rings.
5) MagicBane: Grants MR when wielded, absorbs curses, can engrave
Elbereth, has
useful other attacks. Works best at +7. Wizards get it easily by
sacrificing.
6) Spellbook of Magic Missiles: It is very useful for spellcasters. It
does
same damage at XL30 as Grayswandir, or twoweaponing two silver sabers
against
major demons. With the Eye of Aethiopica it becomes even more powerful.
It does
not destroy any object.
7) 20 Silver arrows: For rangers and other class that can get expert at
bows,
but are not able to get grayswandir or are not able to use twoweaponing
silver
sabers. It causes about same damage as Grayswandir or twoweaponing two
silver
sabers, and can do it from a distance. This is very useful against
major demons
and other silver hating monsters.

My recommendations for the first weapon wish.
1) Archeologist - Grayswandir
2) Barbarian - Grayswandir/ArtifactLongSword
3) Caveman - Grayswandir
4) Healer - Grayswandir
5) Knight - ArtifactLongSword/Grayswandir
6) Monk - Gauntlets of Power (Robe will allow casting of spells)
7) Priest - Grayswandir
8) Ranger - Gauntlets of Power (upto four thrown daggers are deadly).
9) Rogue - Gauntlets of Power (4 daggers with backstab is even more
so).
Wishing for a wand of polymorph to obtain a tooled horn or a leather
drum in
addition to other things is also very useful.
10) Samurai - ArtifactLongSword
11) Tourist - Gauntlets of Power for expert thrown daggers/Grayswandir.
12) Valkyrie - ArtifactLongSword
13) Wizard - Spellbook of Magic Missile/Gauntlets of power.

ArtifactLongSword is Excalibur(Lawfuls get it by dipping in fountains
at XL5)
or Frost Brand. Firebrand is only useful very late in the game, by that
time you
would probably not need it. It also burns more items than Frost Brand.

Gauntlets of power are very important for elves(as they cannot get more
than 18
strength) and also quite important for gnomes and orcs, which cannot
get more
than 18/50. At 18 you get only 2 extra damage bonus and at 18/50 you
get only 3
extra damage bonus. If you are two weaponing or using expert thrown
daggers or
darts, it matters quite a bit 6-10 points of extra damage.

An early gauntlets of power can make a lot of difference for a
character,
making it a good wish. But it is not good for spellcasters which don't
have
robes.


Wand of Wishing
---------------
Strategy for a wand of wishing is different than getting a random wish
from
fountains (not really recommended), thrones, magic lamps, and smoky
potions.
A WoW is an item that can allow you to score your first ascension, if
used
properly. It should not be wasted.

The first wish should always be 2 blessed scrolls of charging if scroll
of
charging has not been identified. Otherwise it should be a magic
marker. This
will allow you to use the full wand completely. It is important to
identify it
if possible, but don't waste time in doing that. There is a 1 in 127
chance
that you will wrest out the last charge when trying to zap an empty
wand.

For the next two wishes you do not know whether they will be your last
wish,
but you will know if it was the last wish. If it is the last wish then
wish
using the above guidelines. Otherwise you know there are more wishes
left.

Next wish should be for SDSM so that you can cover up reflection. It is
also
better than "oR because it leaves the amulet slot for something else.

Wishing for Monk is very different. They get PR easily, Sokoban has
"oR. The
only thing left is Magic Resistance, but they cannot use CoMR, because
that
would replace the Robe, without which they cannot spellcast very well.
So they
must wait for HP 40 before wishing for the EoA. For them the best wish
very
really on is Gauntlets of power. Magic Markers are not that useful very
early
on because they require blank scrolls. And you should only blank
identified
scrolls. It is easy to blank scrolls in pools created by pickaxing a
fountain.

Next wish should be blessed tin of green dragon meat, if you don't have
PR.

After this you need one wish for MR, and for Monks one more maybe for
reflection. You also need to save one more wish for Magic Marker.

Now you must wish for the weapon. The best weapon depends on your role,
as
noted above. But since this is an early wish a GoP should be given a
higher
priority than an artifact weapon. Except for wizard and healer
everybody can
use it. Even for these classes at very high intelligence or wisdom
levels it
could be worn with very little increase in failure rate. For Wizards
Magic
Missile is a special spell, which will allow it to be cast. While for
Healer
most healing spells are emergency (and these are the only ones he is
not
restricted in). Later when they have obtained their maximum protection
and
killed the minetown priest (via a buff pet) it can be worn more easily.

Beyond this point it becomes fuzzy as now it depends on what you need
most
now. You may want to wish for enchant armour or weapon if you cannot
find them
anywhere. A wizard may write them easily when extremely lucky. Or you
may wish
for a bag of holding, or even a blessed figurine of an Archon (but be
prepared
for it if turns out to be hostile).

Now you should be strong enough to reach the castle and get the WoW
there
to complete whatever you need there. But you should explore all levels
thoroughly before reaching there. So that you need to wish only the
things that
you could not find anywhere. You may also wish for a Wand of Polymorph
to make
things that you don't have.


Miscellaneous
-------------
When wishing for an item always wish for a +2 or +3 item. Seasoned
players are
divided on what is better. +3 gives more on average but +2 has a better
chance
of being useful immediately.

When wishing for stackable items you should wish for 2 items. 2 and 3
give
similar items on average but 2 is better chance to be more useful now.



